<div class="general-white-block-email">
  <body class="email">

    <h1>MicroNet Analysis Results</h1>

    <p>Hello,</p>

    <% if @analysis_failures.present? %>
      <p>
        Attached are the results that MicroNet completed successfully.
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <p>
        Attached are the results from your completed MicroNet analysis.
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <% if @optimized_tss.present? %>

      <h3>MicroNet Adjusted This Job</h3>

      <p>
        MicroNet first tried your selected setting. The
        <%= @optimized_tss.size == 1 ? "analysis below needed" : "analyses below needed" %>
        a larger time step size to finish, so MicroNet reran
        <%= @optimized_tss.size == 1 ? "it" : "them" %> and completed
        <%= @optimized_tss.size == 1 ? "it" : "them" %> successfully.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <% @optimized_tss.each do |analysis, info| %>

          <li>
            <strong><%= analysis %></strong><br>
            Started with time step size:
            <strong><%= info[:requested] %></strong><br>
            Completed using time step size:
            <strong><%= info[:used] %></strong>

            <% if info[:high_impact] %>
              <br>
              <em>
                This is a high time step size, so subtle or rapid growth
                changes may be harder to detect.
              </em>
            <% end %>
          </li>

        <% end %>
      </ul>

      <p>
        This does not change your uploaded data or the groups you selected. It
        only means the listed analysis was fit on a coarser set of time points
        to reduce memory use. If you need the highest temporal resolution,
        rerun with a smaller time step size on a system with more memory.
      </p>

    <% end %>

    <% if @analysis_failures.present? %>

      <h3>Some Analyses Could Not Be Completed</h3>

      <p>
        MicroNet completed the attached results, but the
        <%= @analysis_failures.size == 1 ? "analysis below could" : "analyses below could" %>
        not be completed.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <% @analysis_failures.each do |failure| %>

          <li>
            <strong><%= failure[:analysis] %></strong><br>
            <%= failure[:message] %>

            <% if failure[:attempted_tss].present? %>
              <br>
              Time step sizes tried:
              <strong><%= failure[:attempted_tss].join(", ") %></strong>
            <% end %>
          </li>

        <% end %>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Your uploaded data was not changed. You can still use the attached
        results from the analyses that completed successfully.
      </p>

    <% end %>

    <p>
      For more information, check out the papers under the Resources page
      of MicroNet.
    </p>

    <p>
      Thank you for using MicroNet!
    </p>

  </body>
</div>
